{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — the three typographic voices.
  Source: BRANDING/Typography/"HA Typography Rules _ READ ME.pdf"

    IDENTIFY  Porter Medium              house name, headings, navigation   (uppercase A-Z only)
    NARRATE   Junicode Medium / Italic   editorial copy, headlines, quotations
    RECORD    Noto Sans Mono Condensed   specifications, provenance, dates, credits

  Porter is supplied as desktop .otf only and its web licence is unresolved (risk R1),
  so --ha-font-identify currently carries Junicode. When the licence lands: upload
  ha-porter-medium.woff2 to assets and tick "Porter webfont licence confirmed" in
  Theme settings. That is the entire swap — no section code changes.

  Font files are Latin-subset variable WOFF2 built from the Brand Assets originals:
    Junicode  1.1 MB -> 75 KB   (wght 300-700 retained, wdth/ENLA axes pinned)
    Noto Mono 400 KB -> 12 KB
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Junicode";
    src: url({{ 'ha-junicode.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 300 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Junicode";
    src: url({{ 'ha-junicode-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 300 700;
    font-style: italic;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Noto Sans Mono Condensed";
    src: url({{ 'ha-noto-mono-cond.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  {%- if settings.ha_porter_licensed -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Porter";
    src: url({{ 'ha-porter-medium.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  {%- endif -%}

  :root {
    --ha-font-identify: {% if settings.ha_porter_licensed %}"Porter", {% endif %}"Junicode", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --ha-font-narrate:  "Junicode", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --ha-font-record:   "Noto Sans Mono Condensed", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;

    /* override Luxe's font_picker-generated families */
    --font-heading-family: var(--ha-font-identify);
    --font-body-family:    var(--ha-font-narrate);
    --font-accent-family:  var(--ha-font-record);

    /* Luxe derives these from the old Swiss 721 font picker (weight 400).
       The brand book sets Junicode body copy and editorial display at Medium. */
    --font-body-weight: 500;
    --font-body-weight-bold: 700;
    --font-body-style: normal;
  }

  /* IDENTIFY — brand book: uppercase only, tracking +20 to +80, line height 90-110% */
  .ha-identify {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-identify);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* NARRATE — brand book: body line height 140-155%, tracking 0 to +10 */
  .ha-narrate {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-narrate);
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
  }

  /* RECORD — brand book: uppercase labels, tabular numerals, left aligned */
  .ha-record {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-record);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* Navigation is an IDENTIFY surface per the typography rules ("house identification,
     principal headings, navigation, collection titles"). Luxe's base.css assigns
     --font-accent-family to .header-bar-inner with !important, which would put the
     nav in the RECORD voice; these selectors are more specific, so they win.
     Buttons and other interface detail are left on RECORD, which the rules allow. */
  .hdr-nav-primary-level-ul a,
  .nav-ul--primary a,
  .nav-ul--secondary a {
    font-family: var(--ha-font-identify) !important;
  }

  /* Wordmark. Colour comes from `color` because the SVG paints with currentColor:
     Inkstone on light grounds, Chalk Blue on dark. Logo rules give a 220px digital
     minimum width — below that the framed House Symbol must be used instead. */
  .ha-wordmark {
    display: block;
    width: 220px;
    max-width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1225.9 / 301.7;
    color: var(--ha-inkstone);
  }
  .ha-wordmark--invert { color: var(--ha-chalk-blue); }
{% endstyle %}
